import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];Q=[]
def q(ref,text,correct,wrong,explanation):
 opts=[correct]+wrong;random.Random(250500+len(Q)).shuffle(opts)
 Q.append(dict(id=f'MAY-{len(Q)+1:02}',question=text,options=opts,answer=opts.index(correct),explanation=explanation,ref=f'MY25-{ref:03}'))
q(1,'Which statement correctly interprets the May 2025 provisional GDP release?','6.5% was the FY2024–25 real GDP growth estimate.',['6.5% was May 2025 monthly growth.','7.4% was the full-year growth estimate.','GVA and GDP are necessarily identical.'],'The release reported annual real GDP growth of 6.5% and Q4 growth of 7.4%, using that release vintage.')
q(2,'What was announced in May regarding the India–UK FTA?','Conclusion of negotiations, distinct from subsequent treaty implementation.',['Immediate universal duty-free entry for every product.','A general income-tax exemption for every migrant.','Replacement of WTO rules for all Indian trade.'],'Negotiation conclusion, signature and entry into force are different milestones. Social-security contribution arrangements are not general tax exemptions.')
q(3,'India–Chile terms of reference primarily represent:','An agreed framework for negotiations.',['The completion of all CEPA tariff concessions.','A common currency.','A fully operative customs union.'],'Terms of reference set scope; they do not establish that a CEPA has entered into force.')
q(4,'RoDTEP is best understood as:','Remission of eligible embedded taxes not refunded elsewhere.',['A guaranteed purchase of every export consignment.','An exemption from all foreign import duties.','A cash grant unrelated to embedded levies.'],'Its objective is remission of embedded duties and taxes, subject to eligibility and rates. May restoration for categories took effect from June.')
q(5,'Under revised CGSS provisions, ₹20 crore refers to:','The stated maximum guarantee cover per borrower.',['A universal grant to every startup.','The minimum capital for all firms.','A cancellation of every startup debt.'],'Guarantees support eligible lending and do not remove borrower repayment duties or underwriting requirements.')
q(6,'Does an MSP announcement establish that all output is procured?','No; procurement access and actual purchases are separate.',['Yes, every farmer must sell all output to the Union.','Yes, private trade is automatically prohibited.','Only if the crop is grown in Andhra Pradesh.'],'Announced support prices do not themselves prove universal procurement or a legal buying obligation for every unit.')
q(7,'Which terms are explicitly described in the 28 May MISS continuation release?','Eligible crop KCC loans up to ₹3 lakh at 7%, with prompt-repayment incentive.',['Every agricultural loan up to ₹5 lakh at zero interest.','All borrowers receive a 1.5% final rate.','No repayment conditions apply.'],'The dated release retains the structure; the February Budget enhancement announcement must not be silently substituted for May operational terms.')
q(8,'The Draft Registration Bill consultation proves which of the following?','Proposed registration reforms were opened for public feedback.',['The 1908 Act was already repealed by the draft.','Every registered document has guaranteed indefeasible title.','Every land dispute is resolved automatically online.'],'A draft is not enacted law, and document registration is not universally a conclusive title guarantee.')
q(9,'A climate-finance taxonomy primarily:','Classifies activities according to defined climate criteria.',['Automatically sanctions a bank loan.','Creates a carbon credit for every classified project.','Bans all industrial transition investment.'],'Classification can guide finance but is not itself loan approval or credit issuance.')
q(10,'Who chairs the Payments Regulatory Board under the 2025 framework?','RBI Governor.',['Union Home Secretary.','Chairperson of SEBI.','Comptroller and Auditor General.'],'The RBI Governor chairs it; the board should not be confused with the Monetary Policy Committee.')
q(11,'The May FPI corporate-debt relaxation should be read as:','Removal of specified general-route limits, not every debt-investment condition.',['Abolition of all foreign-exchange regulation.','Mandatory foreign purchase of government bonds.','A ban on all short-term debt.'],'Investor-level sublimits and aggregate/regulatory conditions are distinct. Avoid treating a targeted relaxation as total deregulation.')
q(12,'A SHAKTI coal linkage is primarily concerned with:','Access to a coal supply allocation.',['Direct household electricity subsidy.','Ownership of a distribution company.','A universal exemption from emission rules.'],'A fuel linkage differs from a PPA and does not guarantee plant profitability or remove other regulatory duties.')
q(14,'Why does the May Vanashakti note require a legal chronology warning?','Later recall and subsequent proceedings mean the May holding is not a timeless current-law certificate.',['Every Supreme Court judgment expires after a month.','The case concerned only GST.','All existing clearances were necessarily cancelled.'],'The historical May decision protected previously granted ECs and was followed by further litigation. Read current binding orders before relying on the rule today.')
q(15,'What is the approved total outlay described for ITI upgradation?','₹60,000 crore across central, state and industry shares.',['₹60,000 crore entirely spent in May.','₹10,000 crore entirely from trainees.','₹20,000 crore entirely from RBI.'],'The scheme comprises ₹30,000 crore central, ₹20,000 crore state and ₹10,000 crore industry shares; approval is not expenditure.')
q(16,'Which feature distinguishes a virtual PPA in the May draft?','No physical electricity exchange between its contracting parties.',['It requires a dedicated private wire in every case.','It eliminates all market-price risk.','It permits unlimited double counting of RECs.'],'VPPAs separate financial arrangements and environmental attributes from direct physical supply. The May document was a draft.')
q(17,'TRAI’s May satellite-spectrum document should be described as:','Recommendations, distinct from adopted assignment conditions.',['An automatic licence for every company.','A ban on non-geostationary satellites.','A law passed by Parliament.'],'A regulator’s recommendations do not prove that all proposed charges and terms have been adopted.')
q(18,'What benefit cap is described in the road-accident treatment scheme?','Up to ₹1.5 lakh and seven days from the accident, at designated hospitals.',['Unlimited lifetime treatment at any facility.','₹15 lakh for every monthly admission.','Only preventive screening, not trauma care.'],'The amount, time and designated-facility conditions all matter; access depends on implementation.')
q(19,'The ₹58,000-crore Amaravati event package represented:','A mix of inaugurations, dedications and foundation-stage projects.',['Only completed capital-city buildings.','Only projects already fully paid for.','A single hospital procurement.'],'Event totals must not be mistaken for expenditure or completed operational infrastructure.')
q(20,'Which condition in IBM’s May Quantum Valley announcement is important?','On-site deployment remained subject to licences and definitive agreements.',['156 qubits proved universal fault-tolerant computation.','Cloud access meant the on-site computer was installed.','The release guaranteed quantum advantage on all workloads.'],'IBM distinguished cloud-resource access from the envisioned physical installation and explicitly noted conditions.')
q(21,'Nagayalanka’s May development concerned:','Foundation laying for a missile test range.',['Commissioning of a civilian airport.','Commercial manufacture of every DRDO missile.','A new foreign embassy.'],'A test range provides instrumentation and testing infrastructure; foundation laying is not commissioning.')
q(22,'Which chronology is correct for YogAndhra?','May campaign launch preceded the June International Yoga Day event.',['The June event occurred before the May campaign.','The campaign began in January 2024.','All June attendance figures are May outcomes.'],'Preparation and final mass-event participation are different milestones and should not be backdated.')
q(23,'What was the reported PSLV-C61/EOS-09 outcome on 18 May?','Mission not accomplished following a third-stage anomaly.',['Satellite successfully deployed and delivering operational data.','First-stage cancellation before liftoff.','A completed lunar landing.'],'The launch occurred, but initial ISRO statements said mission objectives were not accomplished. Preliminary cause reports are not final findings.')
q(24,'Which pairing is correct?','DRR Dhan 100 (Kamala) — ICAR-IIRR, Hyderabad.',['Pusa DST Rice 1 — RBI.','Kamala — a space telescope.','Pusa DST Rice 1 — a wheat-only programme.'],'Kamala was developed from Samba Mahsuri by IIRR; Pusa DST Rice 1 was developed by IARI from MTU 1010.')
q(25,'WHA adoption of the Pandemic Agreement in May meant:','Further annex and treaty-law steps still remained.',['It immediately bound every WHO member automatically.','WHO gained unlimited authority to order national lockdowns.','Ratification was legally impossible.'],'Adoption, opening for signature, ratification and entry into force are separate legal stages.')
q(26,'A private member in Parliament is:','An MP who is not a minister.',['Only a nominated MP.','Only a member of the opposition.','Any employee of a private company.'],'The sponsor’s ministerial status defines the category; PMBs do not automatically escape whips or anti-defection law.')
q(27,'Which denominator is used for the unemployment rate?','Labour force.',['Total population in every case.','Only employed persons.','Number of registered factories.'],'UR is unemployed as a share of the labour force; LFPR and WPR use population denominators. Reference periods and age groups also matter.')
q(32,'Which treaty–function pairing is correct?','Rotterdam — prior informed consent for listed chemicals.',['Basel — global interest-rate coordination.','Stockholm — administration of shipping routes.','Rotterdam — regulation of all nuclear fuel.'],'Basel concerns hazardous-waste movement, Rotterdam PIC procedures and Stockholm persistent organic pollutants. Consent is not a blanket ban.')
q(34,'India’s 0.685 HDI value in HDR 2025 refers to:','2023 data in that report.',['May 2025 monthly observations.','The state HDI of Andhra Pradesh.','An unemployment rate.'],'A report’s publication year differs from its underlying data year. HDI combines health, education and income dimensions.')
q(35,'Which demographic denominator pairing is correct?','MMR — maternal deaths per 100,000 live births.',['CBR — births per 100 population.','IMR — deaths per 100,000 total population.','MMR — maternal deaths per 1,000 employed women.'],'CBR uses 1,000 population; IMR 1,000 live births; MMR 100,000 live births. The source’s CBR ×100 formula needs correction.')
q(37,'Why is a customised infant gene-editing case not a universal cure?','Individual evidence does not establish broad or long-term efficacy and safety.',['Somatic editing is necessarily inherited by all offspring.','A single case automatically licenses every application.','CPS1 is a container-shipping code.'],'The therapy targeted a specific variant in liver cells. Generalisation requires appropriate evidence, regulation and follow-up.')
assert len(Q)==30
(R/'data/may-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
